{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1780883811, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "fairchem-mcp alloy design"}
[0.742535, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mfairchem-mcp\u001b[0m — alloy design, live (elastic · hull · screen)\r\n\u001b[2m(every number below is from the real engine; AUTO)\u001b[0m\r\n[calculator] EMT (fast/qualitative; set FAIRCHEM_MCP_EXAMPLE_MODEL for UMA)\r\n"]
[0.742932, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  BEAT 1  ·  Elastic tensor — how stiff is a crystal?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» Strain the cell in each Voigt direction, read the stress, fit C_ij. Start from fcc Cu relaxed to its equilibrium lattice.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.784749, "o", "\u001b[33m  ▶ start_relaxation(relax_cell=True, fmax=0.01)   # equilibrium cell first\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.423588, "o", "\u001b[33m  ▶ start_elastic_scan(n_strains=7, max_strain=0.01)  → returns immediately\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.950877, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → deformation 1/42  (2%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.48102, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → deformation 10/42  (24%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.01047, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → deformation 19/42  (45%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.540537, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → deformation 27/42  (64%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.073787, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → deformation 36/42  (86%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.602863, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m    ← C11,C12,C44 = 172, 115, 90 GPa\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.999258, "o", "\u001b[2m    ← K=134  G=57  E=149 GPa   ν=0.31\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.391829, "o", "\u001b[2m    ← Pugh G/K=0.42 (ductile)   Born-stable=True\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.791881, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» EMT Cu lands right on experiment (C11≈168, C12≈121, C44≈75; ν≈0.34), and Pugh < 0.57 correctly calls copper ductile.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.657486, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  BEAT 2  ·  Convex hull — which alloy compositions are stable?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» Build the Cu-Au line: pure Cu, pure Au, and the Cu3Au / CuAu / CuAu3 orderings. Formation energy is referenced to the pure metals.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.703578, "o", "\u001b[33m  ▶ start_convex_hull(relax=True, relax_cell=True)  # 5 compositions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.498989, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → evaluate 2/5  (40%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.766941, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → evaluate 3/5  (60%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.037064, "o", "\u001b[2m    get_status → evaluate 5/5  (100%)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.307165, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m    phase    x_Au  Ef (eV/at)  above hull  stable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    Cu       0.00     +0.0000      0.0000\u001b[0m\u001b[32m  ★\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    Cu3Au    0.25     -0.0103      0.0000\u001b[0m\u001b[32m  ★\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    CuAu     0.50     -0.0078      0.0000\u001b[0m\u001b[32m  ★\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    CuAu3    0.75     +0.0072      0.0111\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    Au       1.00     +0.0000      0.0000\u001b[0m\u001b[32m  ★\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» On the hull (stable): ['Cu', 'Au', 'Cu3Au', 'CuAu']. Cu3Au and CuAu have negative formation energies — the classic L1₂/L1₀ orderings. CuAu3 sits above.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.181168, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  BEAT 3  ·  Design loop — the stiffest phase that will actually form\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[15.181248, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» Step 1 — gate on stability: keep phases ≤ 0.01 eV/atom above the hull. That prunes ['CuAu3'] and keeps ['Cu', 'Au', 'Cu3Au', 'CuAu'].\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.224739, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» Step 2 — score each survivor's stiffness (relax cell, then elastic scan):\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.486242, "o", "\u001b[2m    ← Cu      E= 149.0  K= 134.1  Pugh=0.42  Born-stable=True\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.092517, "o", "\u001b[2m    ← Au      E=  89.2  K= 174.9  Pugh=0.18  Born-stable=True\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.696893, "o", "\u001b[2m    ← Cu3Au   E= 138.4  K= 145.2  Pugh=0.36  Born-stable=True\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.301987, "o", "\u001b[2m    ← CuAu    E= 112.5  K= 152.9  Pugh=0.27  Born-stable=True\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.69757, "o", "\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» Step 3 — rank by Young's modulus (Born-stable only):\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.747401, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m    winner: Cu  E=149 GPa, K=134 GPa, Pugh=0.42\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    runners-up: Cu3Au (E=138), CuAu (E=112), Au (E=89)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[1m» Stability first, then property — the same loop with a different objective (max K, most ductile, …) is a different design study.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[23.623846, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[1m  Elastic tensor · convex hull · property-driven screen.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m  Steerable jobs, one shared namespace — design as a conversation.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
